plan PackageContract
title   Package routes and supported consumers
status  archived
goal
    Give installed consumers one exact named-export package with preserved environmental boundaries
    and evidence for eventual replacement. This proposed Plan owns routes, public declarations,
    supported hosts, compatibility disposition and promotion conditions. Each capability owns its
    API/type/behavior/proofs; this Plan adds package reachability and cutover obligations. The ten
    former flat Plans and Rewrite Task graph are archived as historical provenance; existing Specs
    remain unchanged. No approval, implementation, physical cleanup, package promotion or product
    cutover is claimed here.
outcomes
    O1  Four isolated routes expose only supported names
        Consumers use named exports with local aliases. The only supported routes are:

        | Route | Consumer purpose |
        | --- | --- |
        | flow-state | Root authoring, application and Runtime APIs |
        | flow-state/react | React provider, actor hooks and passive selection |
        | flow-state/testing | Stories, fixtures, behavior gateway and pure models |
        | flow-state/inspect | Inspection, trace/artifact tooling and behavior comparison |

        Root runtime values are actorRef, app, definition, Diagnostic, Implementation, machine,
        module, resource, runtimeSetup, stream and transaction. Implementation is both value and
        type; its value has exactly succeed, effect and merge. It is not an umbrella package.

        The retained standalone can query is owned by @plan.Statecharts.O3. Its current route
        availability remains governed by the restoration gate below.

        Root public types are Definition, StateToken, EventToken, StateOf, EventOf, Machine,
        MemoryOf, InputOf, RequirementsOf, Resource, Transaction, ActorRef, Module, App,
        RuntimeSetup, Runtime, Implementation and CanonicalKeyInput. Exact operation unions are
        inferred through their named families, not new parallel status aliases.

        Restoration targets remain in scope. They are temporarily omitted until their owners and
        proofs land; this proposal does not activate exports:

        | Route | Deferred restoration names |
        | --- | --- |
        | root values | can, indexedDbStorage, persistence, webStorage |
        | root types | ActorSnapshot, Persistence, PersistenceStorage, PersistenceStorageError |
        | root codec types | PersistenceCodec, PersistenceSlot |
        | root value types | PersistenceValue, PersistenceEntry |
        | root error/path names | FlowDisposeError, FlowPersistenceError, FlowUsageError |
        | root type names continued | FlowPath, FlowUsageCode |
        | React | FlowProvider, useActor, useActorByRef, useView; helper under ReactAndHosts.O3 |
        | testing | behavior, fixture, model, story, FlowStoryExecutionError |

        The inspect route restoration list is closed:

        - analyzeTrace, attachInspectionSink, buildBehaviorContract, compressTraceArtifact,
        createInspectionBufferSink, decompressTraceArtifact, diffBehaviorContracts, diffTrace.
        - exportTraceArtifact, formatInspectionEvent, formatInspectionTimeline,
        formatNoTransitionSummary, formatRehydrationSummary, formatResourceFreshnessReport,
        formatTrace, formatTransactionOverlapSummary.
        - graphOf, importTraceArtifact, inspectActivities, inspectMicrosteps, inspectTransition,
        renderBehaviorContract, renderBehaviorCoverage, renderBehaviorDiff,
        sliceBehaviorContract, summarizeTrace, whyNoTransition.

        React/testing/inspect paths remain published with empty active exports under the temporary
        disposition. Their restoration lists remain obligations. The temporary Runtime shell has
        only app, construct() and ready(); it has no actor, bridge, persistence, lifecycle or
        disposal behavior.

        Temporary ready is Effect<void, ImplementationError>, caches one terminal Exit, and acquires
        providers sequentially once. Full Runtime contracts are future targets under
        @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O3 through @plan.ApplicationsAndActors.O7 and
        @plan.ReactAndHosts.O4. A temporary scaffold cannot prove the complete target.

        Root and non-root routes expose no package-owned flow/test/inspect/hooks namespace objects,
        root builders re-exported from non-root routes, private deep imports, internal service tags,
        stores, orchestrators, ManagedRuntime, boot, harness or public testing/inspection artifact
        types. Consumer-local namespace import aliases do not create a package namespace object.
        Diagnostic rendering guarantees belong to @plan.DiagnosticsContract.O4.
        They add no public route values. React's explicit useShallow
        helper follows its capability owner @plan.ReactAndHosts.O3; it is not a root export.
    O2  Exact declarations and a maintained quickstart reach packed consumers
        Public values/types preserve the owning capability's literal inference, nominal identity,
        unions, field presence, variance, requirement closure and failure channels. Accepted use
        needs no any/assertion erasure, explicit generics or wrappers. StateOf/EventOf/InputOf/
        MemoryOf accept the specified Definition/Machine values. Public declarations contain no
        implementation-only route, recursive config carrier or erased environment requirement.

        Maintain one checked-in quickstart from definition/machine through module/app, runtimeSetup
        and readiness using named exports. It compiles against the packed package and reflects
        accepted API changes. Temporary actor continuation stays explicitly future until its owner
        and proofs land.

        React or Story continuation uses its own route. The supporting [consumer
        example](references/README.md) illustrates the authoring boundary; it is not a
        completed quickstart proof.

        Compile representative small/medium isolated TypeScript consumers, strict and
        isolated-modules settings, isolated declaration emit, packed ESM imports, and React 18/19
        consumers. Exact positive and negative semantic fixtures stay with capability owners.
        Package integration adds import/declaration/runtime reachability and distinct host failure
        cases.

        Do not duplicate every owner's full matrix or make compiler benchmark arithmetic a
        requirement. Recursive carrier rejection must avoid excessive instantiation.
    O3  Replacements remove deleted surfaces and retain environmental compatibility
        DELETE removes without replacement. REPLACE removes the old surface and retains only its
        accepted capability. Neither allows alias, overload, adapter, compatibility namespace,
        parser branch or deprecated wrapper.

        RETAIN preserves only its explicit boundary. HISTORICAL permits provenance, never active
        semantic authority.

        The complete surface disposition is:

        Views and actor identity:

        - DEL-001 DELETE: registered views, View IDs/module.views/lookup, useView(view), view can.
        - DEL-002 DELETE: child actor constructors, inputs, addresses, output, completion and state.
        - DEL-003 DELETE: dynamicMachines, root/dynamic categories, auto roots and runtime.actor.

        Ownership, grammar and operations:

        - DEL-004 REPLACE: handle disposal/active-or-disposed ownership with leases/four lifecycles.
        - DEL-005 REPLACE: initial/flat-only/final/onDone/output/Boolean reentry/conflicting 
        handlers.
        - DEL-006 DELETE: generic activity kits/operation refs/byKey/byLane/entries/enumeration.

        React, Stories and artifacts:

        - DEL-007 REPLACE: recursive sharing/custom equality/comparators with fixed Object.is laws.
        - DEL-008 REPLACE: React shells/root-only hooks/useResource/broad subscriptions/view 
        objects.
        - DEL-009 REPLACE: callable story/with/injection/replay/old commands/mutable 
        harness/runners.
        - DEL-010 REPLACE: mutable v1 boot, root/child/final wire, replay inspect and old Story 
        schemas.
        - DEL-011 HISTORICAL: former contracts, compatibility/phase/task documents as provenance.

        Retained environmental and runtime boundaries:

        - RET-001 RETAIN: four routes, ESM/import conditions, Effect identity and React 
        compatibility.
        - RET-002 RETAIN: synchronous send, production mailbox, scoped stores, fencing, 
        Cause/cleanup.
        - RET-003 RETAIN: exact resource and transaction status discriminants.
        - RET-004 RETAIN: canonical key/getState/getData, transition actions and accepted O/P/K.
        - RET-005 RETAIN: FlowProvider, revised actor hooks and passive useView.

        DEL-002 includes child lifecycle, persistence, snapshots, Story/model forms and addressing.
        DEL-003 includes ID-bearing local creation and dynamic-root persistence. DEL-005 retains
        recursive defaults/exact reentry/ordinary terminal-looking leaves and event actions.

        DEL-006 retains exact named families. DEL-009 removes perform/deliver/receive/simulate/
        flush/settle/setTime/final/replay, bare-App/live-Runtime input and focused overrides;
        @plan.StoriesAndModels.O1 and @plan.StoriesAndModels.O3 own accepted replacements. DEL-010
        also removes fabricated fields, duplicate formatters and arbitrary scenario commands.

        Deleted inputs fail before actor creation, memory/store mutation, acquisition, event
        publication, external work or evidence. Accepted replacement and deleted surfaces cannot
        coexist in installed code, declarations or current product guidance. Deleted names may
        appear in this ledger, historical provenance or negative absence proofs only. Reference
        consumers rewrite old calls; folder layout alone is not a public deletion rule.
    O4  Promotion waits for owner proofs and actual consumer gates
        Complete the replacement only after capability owner proofs and required package/consumer/
        browser/installed-CLI gates pass with explicit receipts. A focused typecheck, source scan,
        generated output or green frozen-package check cannot establish rewrite behavior.

        Proving applications exercise real supported paths:

        - Todo Essentials: recursive states, refs/leases, actions/operations, React views, fixtures,
        Stories, checkpoints and TestClock.
        - Incident Console: exact bindings, transaction conflicts, streams, remote leases,
        inspection, diagnostics, installed CLI/artifacts and browser lifetime.
        - Hydrated Offline Notes: request isolation, context-closed persistence, first-render
        consistency, outbox/reconnect/disposal, exact restore and trusted seeding.
        - An application-authored bounded feed: dropping/coalescing without Flow pressure options.
        React 18/19 and isolated TypeScript consumers supply independent integration coverage.

        Before cutover, map every affected old clause, symbol, overload, registry, consumer, proof
        and Task as DELETE/REPLACE/RETAIN/HISTORICAL or unchanged. Keep every live obligation under
        one capability owner. Source cleanup waits for mapped proofs and one complete no-consumer/
        no-residue audit.

        Historical files and frozen packages stay unchanged in this proposal. Product documentation
        and Task status retain their owners. Physical cleanup, root gate retargeting and product
        cutover remain later authorization gates, not work authorized by creation or approval of
        this Plan set.
decisions
    D1  Each capability owns its whole consumer contract
        API, types, observable behavior and Verification stay together. Shared laws are referenced
        once at their owner. There is no separate PublicSurface, Types or Verification contract
        required to interpret the new capability set. Dependency phase ordering belongs to Tasks.
    D2  Integration proves package reachability
        One decisive production-owner proof covers each semantic invariant. Packed, browser, Story
        and installed-process checks add reachability or distinct races/failures/wire boundaries.
        They do not repeat the full semantic matrix without a distinct observable failure.
constraints
    C1  Preserve the accepted platform and portable bytes
        The development baseline is Node 22.18+, nub 0.7.5, TypeScript 7.0.2, Vite Plus and Effect
        4.0.0-rc.112. Preserve one Effect peer identity and supported React 18/19 boundaries. Shared
        definition, ref, key, persistence, artifact and CLI byte codecs use host-neutral
        ECMAScript/Web APIs and WHATWG TextEncoder.

        Reject lone surrogates with isWellFormed or an equivalent fallback. Do not use Node Buffer,
        silent replacement, UTF-16 byte counts, runtime-specific or second handwritten encoders in
        the shared package contract.

        Equal accepted input produces equal bytes/identities on Node, Bun, Deno, Chromium, Gecko
        and WebKit. Full Unicode/limit vectors run on pinned Node; compact same-codec portability
        vectors run on the other exact recorded host versions. No exact private Runtime topology,
        numeric compiler-growth budget or full vector repetition on every host is imposed.
    C2  Preserve final gates without claiming them passed
        Build package/CLI output through pinned commands and regenerate docs from real entrypoints.
        Never hand-edit dist or generated docs. Rewrite focused gates target flow-state-rewrite:
        check:types, focused tests/lint, build, check:build-output, check:packed-consumers and
        check:static-harness as applicable.

        Product consumer/browser/published-package gates remain required before promotion. Root nub
        run build/docs:build/verify must target the replacement before they can establish
        replacement workspace closure. Current frozen-package gates are migration evidence only.

        Actual runs belong in implementation Task records, not Plan status.
    C3  Preserve proposal, source and package boundaries
        This set is proposed pending approval. The former flat Plans and Rewrite Task graph are
        archived as historical provenance; existing Specs remain unchanged and their archived Plan
        references still resolve. No source contract, reference implementation, historical behavior
        or proof receipt supplies missing new semantics or proves completion.

        Build the greenfield rewrite; packages/flow-state is frozen. User approval of a Plan does
        not authorize commits, pushes, source deletion or product cutover. Missing exact shapes
        remain concrete Questions.
verification
    V1  Routes, exports and packed declaration reachability
        Establish @O1 and @O2 by testing runtime imports and emitted packed declarations for all
        four routes. Active names/value-type duals match the closed lists; deferred names stay
        absent until their owners/proofs restore them. Reject package namespaces, root re-exports
        from non-root routes, private deep imports and deleted public artifacts/authority types.

        Compile the maintained quickstart, strict isolated consumers and React 18/19 against the
        packed build without any/assertion erasure. Planned package gates under @C2; not run here.
    V2  Portable codec and supported-host integration
        Establish @O2 and @C1 with full Node ASCII/2/3/4-byte, 256/257-byte, lone-surrogate and
        composed/decomposed vectors. Run the compiled shared codec on Bun, Deno, Chromium, Gecko
        and WebKit using compact ASCII/multibyte/surrogate/canonical-byte-or-digest vectors. Record
        exact versions and equal accepted bytes; invalid durable input fails before serialization
        or activation. Planned codec/host checks; no portability receipt is claimed.
    V3  Hard deletion, retained boundaries and no residue
        Establish @O3 through runtime export absence, negative packed declarations and behavioral
        submission of removed forms. Every DEL row rejects before side effects; RET rows remain
        reachable through accepted owners. Audit code/docs/consumers/Stories/fixtures/tests/Tasks/
        registries for aliases, adapters, parser branches and deleted-only paths.

        Source scans support but cannot replace runtime/type proofs. Keep one complete mapped final
        audit; ordinary Tasks cover only intersecting removals. Planned audit and owner tests;
        unbuilt.
    V4  Package promotion and proving applications
        Establish @O4 after every owning capability's acceptance and blocking reviews pass. Run the
        proving applications through installed/packed APIs and browser/request/CLI boundaries.
        Record failure/interruption/cleanup cases and distinct integration risks.

        Complete package, declarations, build, docs, consumers, supported browsers and final
        workspace verification against replacement owners; frozen results do not count. Preserve
        live obligations before source cleanup. Later Tasks must identify product owners, retarget
        root build/docs and published/browser gates, and obtain cutover authorization. Record actual
        passing receipts before promotion, source cleanup or cutover. No gate run is claimed.
